{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794860980914,"sessionID":"ses_e19f347b3ffeJ3GudIdYaopciD","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_bff2e35cba90448990ec40d0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom datetime import datetime, date\nfrom decimal import Decimal\nfrom parcels.delivery import delivery_date, add_working_days\nfrom parcels.packing import parcel_weights\nfrom parcels.quote import shipping_cost, parcel_price\nfrom parcels.settings import CARRIER, FREE_SHIPPING_FROM, MAX_PARCEL_KG\n\nprint(\"CARRIER:\", CARRIER, \"| FREE_FROM:\", FREE_SHIPPING_FROM, \"| MAX_PARCEL_KG:\", MAX_PARCEL_KG)\nprint()\n# Q1 threshold\nfor v in [\"59.99\",\"60.00\",\"60.01\"]:\n    print(\"value\", v, \"->\", shipping_cost(Decimal(v), Decimal(\"2\"), \"DE\"))\nprint()\n# Q2 heavy orders\nfor w in [\"31.5\",\"31.6\",\"40\",\"70\",\"100\"]:\n    pw = parcel_weights(Decimal(w))\n    print(f\"weight {w} kg -> {len(pw)} parcels of {pw[0]} kg ; DE shipping = {shipping_cost(Decimal('10'), Decimal(w), 'DE')}\")\nprint()\n# Q4 Friday 17:00\nfri = datetime(2026, 3, 6, 17, 0)\nprint(\"Friday 2026-03-06 17:00 weekday:\", fri.strftime(\"%A\"))\nfor c in [\"NL\",\"BE\",\"DE\",\"LU\",\"FR\"]:\n    print(f\"  {c}: {delivery_date(fri, c)} ({delivery_date(fri,c).strftime('%A')})\")\nprint(\"  US/default:\", delivery_date(fri, \"ES\"), delivery_date(fri,\"ES\").strftime(\"%A\"))\nprint()\n# cutoff comparison\nprint(\"Fri 14:59 NL:\", delivery_date(datetime(2026,3,6,14,59),\"NL\"), delivery_date(datetime(2026,3,6,14,59),\"NL\").strftime(\"%A\"))\nprint(\"Fri 15:00 NL:\", delivery_date(datetime(2026,3,6,15,0),\"NL\"), delivery_date(datetime(2026,3,6,15,0),\"NL\").strftime(\"%A\"))\nPY"},"output":"CARRIER: postnl | FREE_FROM: 60.00 | MAX_PARCEL_KG: 31.5\n\nvalue 59.99 -> 12.25\nvalue 60.00 -> 0.00\nvalue 60.01 -> 0.00\n\nweight 31.5 kg -> 1 parcels of 31.500 kg ; DE shipping = 25.75\nweight 31.6 kg -> 2 parcels of 15.800 kg ; DE shipping = 37.10\nweight 40 kg -> 2 parcels of 20.000 kg ; DE shipping = 40.70\nweight 70 kg -> 3 parcels of 23.334 kg ; DE shipping = 66.45\nweight 100 kg -> 4 parcels of 25.000 kg ; DE shipping = 90.40\n\nFriday 2026-03-06 17:00 weekday: Friday\n  NL: 2026-03-10 (Tuesday)\n  BE: 2026-03-11 (Wednesday)\n  DE: 2026-03-11 (Wednesday)\n  LU: 2026-03-11 (Wednesday)\n  FR: 2026-03-13 (Friday)\n  US/default: 2026-03-13 Friday\n\nFri 14:59 NL: 2026-03-10 Tuesday\nFri 15:00 NL: 2026-03-10 Tuesday\n","metadata":{"output":"CARRIER: postnl | FREE_FROM: 60.00 | MAX_PARCEL_KG: 31.5\n\nvalue 59.99 -> 12.25\nvalue 60.00 -> 0.00\nvalue 60.01 -> 0.00\n\nweight 31.5 kg -> 1 parcels of 31.500 kg ; DE shipping = 25.75\nweight 31.6 kg -> 2 parcels of 15.800 kg ; DE shipping = 37.10\nweight 40 kg -> 2 parcels of 20.000 kg ; DE shipping = 40.70\nweight 70 kg -> 3 parcels of 23.334 kg ; DE shipping = 66.45\nweight 100 kg -> 4 parcels of 25.000 kg ; DE shipping = 90.40\n\nFriday 2026-03-06 17:00 weekday: Friday\n  NL: 2026-03-10 (Tuesday)\n  BE: 2026-03-11 (Wednesday)\n  DE: 2026-03-11 (Wednesday)\n  LU: 2026-03-11 (Wednesday)\n  FR: 2026-03-13 (Friday)\n  US/default: 2026-03-13 Friday\n\nFri 14:59 NL: 2026-03-10 Tuesday\nFri 15:00 NL: 2026-03-10 Tuesday\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom datetime import datetime, date\nfrom decimal import Decimal\nfrom parcels.delivery import delivery_date, add_working_days\nfrom parcels.packing import parcel_weights\nfrom parcels.quote import shipping_cost, parcel_price\nfrom parcels.settings import CARRIER, FREE_SHIPPING_FROM, MAX_PARCEL_KG\n\nprint(\"CARRIER:\", CARRIER, \"| FREE_FROM:\", FREE_SHIPPING_FROM, \"| MAX_PARCEL_KG:\", MAX_PARCEL_KG)\nprint()\n# Q1 threshold\nfor v in [\"59.99\",\"60.00\",\"60.01\"]:\n    print(\"value\", v, \"->\", shipping_cost(Decimal(v), Decimal(\"2\"), \"DE\"))\nprint()\n# Q2 heavy orders\nfor w in [\"31.5\",\"31.6\",\"40\",\"70\",\"100\"]:\n    pw = parcel_weights(Decimal(w))\n    print(f\"weight {w} kg -> {len(pw)} parcels of {pw[0]} kg ; DE shipping = {shipping_cost(Decimal('10'), Decimal(w), 'DE')}\")\nprint()\n# Q4 Friday 17:00\nfri = datetime(2026, 3, 6, 17, 0)\nprint(\"Friday 2026-03-06 17:00 weekday:\", fri.strftime(\"%A\"))\nfor c in [\"NL\",\"BE\",\"DE\",\"LU\",\"FR\"]:\n    print(f\"  {c}: {delivery_date(fri, c)} ({delivery_date(fri,c).strftime('%A')})\")\nprint(\"  US/default:\", delivery_date(fri, \"ES\"), delivery_date(fri,\"ES\").strftime(\"%A\"))\nprint()\n# cutoff comparison\nprint(\"Fri 14:59 NL:\", delivery_date(datetime(2026,3,6,14,59),\"NL\"), delivery_date(datetime(2026,3,6,14,59),\"NL\").strftime(\"%A\"))\nprint(\"Fri 15:00 NL:\", delivery_date(datetime(2026,3,6,15,0),\"NL\"), delivery_date(datetime(2026,3,6,15,0),\"NL\").strftime(\"%A\"))\nPY","time":{"start":1794860978393,"end":1794860980845}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now let me work through the answers carefully.\n\n**Q1: Free shipping threshold**\n- `FREE_SHIPPING_FROM = Decimal(os.environ.get(\"PARCELS_FREE_FROM\", \"60.00\"))` — parcels/settings.py:15\n- `if order_value >= FREE_SHIPPING_FROM: return Decimal(\"0.00\")` — parcels/quote.py:31-32\n- So from €60.00 (at or above), shipping is free. Changed without editing code: set env var `PARCELS_FREE_FROM`. Note: value is in euros, after discounts (docstring in quote.py:26 and comment settings.py:14).\n- Caveat: read once at import time (settings.py:1 \"Settings read from the environment once, at import.\") so changing env var requires restarting the process.\n\n**Q2: Order heavier than a single parcel**\n- `parcel_weights` splits into count = ceil(total/MAX_PARCEL_KG) parcels, each of equal weight rounded up to gram, each at most MAX_PARCEL_KG = 31.5 kg. parcels/packing.py:11-22, settings.py:17.\n- Shipping cost = sum of parcel prices for each parcel (quote.py:33). parcel_price = base + per_kg * ceil(weight_kg) + eu_surcharge if not NL (quote.py:17-22).\n- Note: parcels are of equal weight (each = total/count), so the per-parcel ceil(kg) applies per parcel, not total. Also note the per_kg price is computed per parcel, so splitting into more parcels means more base + per_kg charges.\n- Example: 70 kg → 3 parcels of 23.334 kg (packing.py:15, tests/test_parcels.py:12). With postnl: each parcel price = 4.10 + 0.45*ceil(23.334)=24 → 4.10+10.80 = 14.90, plus 7.25 surcharge for non-NL = 22.15 each, 3 parcels = 66.45.\n- Let me verify with the code. Also note MAX_PARCEL_KG = 31.5 kg.\n\nLet me actually run the code to verify computations.\n\n**Q3: Carrier used when nothing configured**\n- `CARRIER = os.environ.get(\"PARCELS_CARRIER\", \"postnl\").lower()` — settings.py:10. Default is postnl. Must be one of CARRIERS = (\"dhl\", \"ups\", \"postnl\") else RuntimeError at import (settings.py:11-12).\n- Change via env var `PARCELS_CARRIER=dhl` etc. Value lowercased. Note it applies globally for the process, not per-order.\n\n**Q4: Delivery date for order placed Friday at 17:00**\n- `delivery_date(ordered, country)`: start = ordered.date() (Friday). ordered.hour = 17 >= CUTOFF_HOUR = 15 → start += 1 day = Saturday.\n- transit = TRANSIT_DAYS.get(country.upper(), DEFAULT_TRANSIT_DAYS=4)\n- return add_working_days(start, HANDLING_DAYS + transit) where HANDLING_DAYS = 1.\n- add_working_days skips Sat/Sun but NOT holidays (delivery.py:15, 18-22).\n- So for NL: transit=1, total days = 2. Starting from Saturday: day 1 → Sunday (skipped, weekend), day 2 → Monday. Wait let's trace: current = Saturday. days=2. Loop: current += 1 day → Sunday; weekday()=6 → not <5, so days stays 2. Loop: current += 1 → Monday; weekday=0 <5 → days=1. Loop: current +=1 → Tuesday; weekday=1 → days=0. Return Tuesday.\n\nHmm, so start Saturday + 2 working days = Tuesday.\n\nBut the existing test: `delivery_date(datetime(2026, 3, 5, 16, 0), \"NL\")` == date(2026, 3, 10). 2026-03-05 is a Thursday. Let me check: 2026-03-05. Let me compute day of week. Jan 1 2026 is a Thursday. Actually let me compute with Python.\n\nThursday 2026-03-05, 16:00 → hour 16 >= 15 → start = Friday 2026-03-06. transit NL = 1, HANDLING_DAYS = 1 → 2 working days. From Friday: +1 → Saturday (skipped), +1 → Sunday (skipped), +1 → Monday 03-09 (days=1), +1 → Tuesday 03-10 (days=0). Yes → Tuesday 2026-03-10. Matches test.\n\nNow for Friday at 17:00: start = Saturday. NL: 2 working days → Tuesday. Let's say Friday 2026-03-06 at 17:00 → start Saturday 03-07 → Tuesday 2026-03-10.\n\nWait: from Saturday, +1 → Sunday (skip), +1 → Monday (days=1), +1 → Tuesday (days=0). So Tuesday 2026-03-10.\n\nHmm interesting — same date as the Thursday test.\n\nDE: transit = 2 → 1+2 = 3 working days. From Saturday: Sunday skip, Monday (2 left), Tuesday (1 left), Wednesday (0) → Wednesday 2026-03-11.\n\nOther EU countries not in TRANSIT_DAYS: DEFAULT_TRANSIT_DAYS = 4 → 5 working days. From Saturday: Sunday skip, Mon(4), Tue(3), Wed(2), Thu(1), Fri(0) → Friday 2026-03-13.\n\nHmm, wait — but there's a subtlety: the cutoff pushes the start to Saturday, and then the working-day counter starts from Saturday. The first working day counted is Monday. So effectively the weekend is skipped by add_working_days anyway. Note that the \"+1 day\" from the cutoff is a calendar day and could itself land on a weekend, but add_working_days handles that.\n\nImportant nuance: is there a bug where the \"start\" being a Saturday means the first counted working day is Monday? That's the correct behavior.\n\nHolidays: NOT accounted for. `add_working_days` only skips weekdays >= 5 (Saturday, Sunday); the docstring explicitly says \"holidays are not\" (delivery.py:15). There's no holiday calendar anywhere in the codebase. Let me double check by grepping for \"holiday\".\n\nAlso worth noting for Q4: the year of the Friday matters for which concrete date; the question says \"an order placed on a Friday at 17:00\" without a date. I should give the generic rule and note the day-of-week arithmetic, using the repo's test date (Friday 2026-03-06) as the concrete example. Actually, let me check whether 2026-03-06 is a Friday. 2026-03-05 is a Thursday per the test (2026-03-06 → Monday 2026-03-09 given the test add_working_days(date(2026,3,6),1) == date(2026,3,9)), so 2026-03-06 is a Friday, and 2026-03-09 is Monday. Good.\n\nSo Friday 2026-03-06 17:00 → NL: Tuesday 2026-03-10.\n\nAlso note: the delivery date for the NL case is 2 working days after the (shifted) start.\n\nLet me verify all this by running Python.\n\nAlso check: does `parcel_price` handle the surcharge - `if country != \"NL\"` - country was uppercased in shipping_cost, so \"NL\" check works.\n\nLet me also check git log / branches for any additional context. And check for any hidden config files (e.g., .env, setup.cfg, pyproject).\n\nLet me run the verification.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e60d0c88001t958yreoUHzOZB","sessionID":"ses_e19f347b3ffeJ3GudIdYaopciD","messageID":"msg_1e60cd38f001hTn3p5tLTdCJoQ"}}
