{"type":"text","timestamp":1794861017728,"sessionID":"ses_e19f347b3ffeJ3GudIdYaopciD","part":{"id":"prt_1e60da42c001PqQ8UMz04wf0nK","messageID":"msg_1e60da16f001WPTe98pIWBYugz","sessionID":"ses_e19f347b3ffeJ3GudIdYaopciD","type":"text","text":"Wrote `ANSWERS.md` at the project root; no code changed and the test suite still passes.\n\n**Summary of the answers (all verified by running the code):**\n\n1. **Free shipping from €60.00** (inclusive) — `FREE_SHIPPING_FROM` in `parcels/settings.py:15`, applied at `parcels/quote.py:31-32`. Change it via the `PARCELS_FREE_FROM` env var (no code edit); the value is after discounts, EU-only, and read once at import.\n2. **Heavy orders are split, not rejected** — no maximum total weight. `parcel_weights()` makes `ceil(kg / 31.5)` equal-weight parcels rounded up to the gram (`parcels/packing.py:20-22`, `parcels/settings.py:17`) and shipping is charged per parcel (`parcels/quote.py:33`); 70 kg → 3 × 23.334 kg → €66.45 to DE with postnl.\n3. **`postnl` is the default carrier** — `parcels/settings.py:10`. Set `PARCELS_CARRIER` to `dhl`/`ups`/`postnl`; an invalid value raises `RuntimeError` at import (`parcels/settings.py:11-12`). The choice is process-wide.\n4. **Friday 17:00** → cutoff pushes the start to Saturday (`parcels/delivery.py:11,26-28`), then working days are counted: NL → Tue 2026-03-10, DE/BE/LU → Wed 2026-03-11, other EU → Fri 2026-03-13. **Weekends are skipped** (`parcels/delivery.py:20`), but **public holidays are not** — the docstring says so explicitly (`parcels/delivery.py:15`) and there is no holiday calendar in the repo.","time":{"start":1794861016108,"end":1794861017727}}}
